    LLM: "Game: London Lowball. Seven Card Stud Lowball, Pot-Limit. 2-8 players. 2 down, 1 up initially; 4th-6th up, 7th down. Highest door card brings in. Lowest hand acts first. Ace-to-five lowball: A-2-3-4-5 best. Straights/flushes don't count. Pairs are bad. Best 5 of 7 cards play.",
    Player: "Welcome to London Lowball! This is Seven Card Stud where the LOWEST hand wins. A-2-3-4-5 (the Wheel) is the absolute nutsâ€”straights and flushes don't count against you. Highest card on board pays the bring-in, then lowest hand acts first. It's Pot-Limit, so be carefulâ€”those bets can escalate quickly!",
    objective: 'Form the lowest possible 5-card hand. Straights and Flushes ARE NOT counted (California/A-5 Lowball rules).',
    gameplay: "1. **Bring-In**: The player with the HIGHEST door card (1st up card) must pay a mandatory bring-in bet. 2. **Betting Rounds**: Five rounds of betting (starting after 3rd street). 3. **Showdown**: Players reveal 7 cards; best 5-card 'Low' hand wins.",
